Gate suites live in `tests/`, or next to the gate they drive when the suite runs
it as a subprocess with no repo fixture. Both directories run in `task
lint:invariants` and the CI python-tests job.

A verification script gets one of two suite shapes. A script that needs a live
cluster to run at all is tested per function, by extracting the function under
test and driving it directly — `scripts/test_deploy_verify_script.py` does this for
`deploy-verify.sh`. A script that can run start to finish is tested end to end
instead, against stub `kubectl`, `curl` and `sleep` executables placed on `PATH`
and a JSON fixture describing what each stub should return.

`kubernetes/infrastructure/observability/loki/host-log-staleness.yaml` is
generated the same way: it ships with the cluster-wide arm only, and `task
flux:sync-host-log-staleness` adds one alert per host once the inventory is
filled in. `task lint:repo-sync` is red until that first run.

`hosts.env` ships empty: the host roster is the one thing the template cannot
guess. Until you fill in `ansible/inventories/prod/hosts.yml` and run `task
hosts:sync`, any task that iterates over a host list stops with an explicit
"empty — run task hosts:sync" message rather than doing nothing quietly.
